What I would NOT work on yet

I'd deliberately push these down:

❌ UI

Not yet.

The CLI is giving you incredible visibility into the internals right now.

Build the brain first.

❌ TTS/STT

Also not yet.

Voice makes Atlas feel more alive, but doesn't make the underlying assistant better.

❌ API server

Useful eventually, especially for your future UI/mobile access, but not your immediate bottleneck.

❌ Full autonomous goals

Way later.

That's the stuff we were philosophically discussing. You want the underlying architecture capable of safely supporting agency before giving Atlas meaningful autonomy.

❌ "Feeling Alive"

Also later.

Ironically, the systems you're building now are what will eventually make this possible.